WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.613
Medicine reminders, set up straight from
the prescription.

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.886
Interviews and surveys showed people knew
what was good for them. They just

3
00:00:08.886 --> 00:00:09.576
weren't consistent.

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.992
A health records app could already read
prescriptions, but reminders still had

5
00:00:13.992 --> 00:00:15.888
to be typed in by hand.

6
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.666
The redesign connects the two. Right after
reading, it asks one question: set

7
00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:23.255
reminders for these medicines?

8
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:27.767
Each medicine arrives filled in. Only
what's missing is left to add.

9
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:33.301
The mistake not to repeat: no testing with
real users. A reminder that looks

10
00:00:33.301 --> 00:00:35.801
like a phone call only adds confusion.

11
00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:39.400
[Instrumental music]
